@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<main class="policy-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 29, 2026</p>

    <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how Axert University handles information
        through AxertLMS, its learning management system. It applies to visitors,
        students, and staff using the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Information collected and stored</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Account information, including name, email address, role, account status,
            and credentials needed to authenticate an AxertLMS account.
        </li>
        <li>
            Student and academic information submitted to or generated by the LMS,
            including registration details, enrollment, class and section
            information, assignments, submissions, grades, and related records.
        </li>
        <li>
            Technical and diagnostic information in application and hosting logs,
            which may include request details, timestamps, and error information
            used to operate, secure, and troubleshoot the service.
        </li>
        <li>
            When you use Google sign-in, Google provides a Google account identifier,
            email address, verification status, and basic profile information. The
            app uses these details to authenticate you and associate the Google
            account with an AxertLMS account.
        </li>
        <li>
            If you separately connect Google Calendar, the app receives OAuth tokens
            and permission to read upcoming events from your primary calendar and
            create calendar events for LMS features. OAuth tokens are encrypted
            before being stored by the application.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How information is used</h2>
    <p>
        Information is used to authenticate accounts; manage student, teacher, and
        staff roles and registration; deliver classes, assignments, submissions,
        grades, and other LMS functions; protect and troubleshoot the service; and,
        only when you connect it, provide Google Calendar features.
    </p>

    <h2>Google API data use and sharing</h2>
    <p>
        Google user data is used only to provide the sign-in or Google Calendar
        feature that you requested, to secure and maintain that feature, and as
        otherwise permitted by applicable law. Calendar data is not used for
        advertising, sold, or used to build advertising profiles.
    </p>
    <p>
        Google data is not shared with third parties except as necessary to provide
        and host AxertLMS, when you direct the app to create an event in your
        calendar, with your consent, for security or legal reasons, or as otherwise
        described in this policy. Hosting and database providers process information
        to operate the service and are expected to protect it.
    </p>
    <p>
        AxertLMS's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres
        to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>Storage, retention, and deletion</h2>
    <p>
        AxertLMS application records are stored in the database configured for the
        service. Google OAuth tokens are stored in encrypted form. Account and
        academic records are retained while needed to provide the LMS and administer
        educational records, subject to applicable institutional and legal
        requirements. Diagnostic logs are retained according to the hosting and
        service configuration.
    </p>
    <p>
        You may revoke AxertLMS's Google access in your
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Account connections</a>.
        To request access, correction, or deletion of information held by AxertLMS,
        contact the address below. Requests are reviewed by the service operator;
        some academic or administrative records may need to be retained. Revoking
        Google access does not by itself delete AxertLMS account or academic records.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
        AxertLMS uses safeguards intended to protect information, including
        encrypted storage of Google OAuth tokens and restricted account access.
        No online service can guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>Children and student records</h2>
    <p>
        AxertLMS is an educational service and may process student information.
        Student accounts are subject to applicable school policies and laws.
        Parents, guardians, or students with questions about a student record should
        contact the school or the service contact below.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        This policy may be updated when the service or its data practices change.
        The updated date at the top of the page will be revised when changes are
        made.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        For privacy questions or requests, contact
        <a href="mailto:kurtcandrejo@gmail.com">kurtcandrejo@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
</main>

<style>
    .policy-page {
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .policy-page h1,
    .policy-page h2 {
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .policy-page a {
        color: #8ab4f8;
    }
</style>
